course: dictionary
lesson: 14252
title: Neighbourly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one. The word here is neighbourly. Its first meaning is friendly and helpful, the way a good neighbour is. «It was very neighbourly of Mrs Okafor to bring us soup when we were ill.» Bringing soup to a sick family is a kind, helpful thing, so neighbourly means kind and helpful here.
explain: Look for the clues. «Tom and his dad had a neighbourly chat over the garden fence.» A chat over a fence is friendly and relaxed, so a neighbourly chat is a friendly talk between neighbours. The words around the word tell you its feeling.
explain: Neighbourly can also be a formal word, used in serious writing about neighbours as a group. «The council wants good neighbourly relations on our street.» Here it means the way neighbours get along with each other. Try the meaning in the sentence: does «good friendly relations» fit? Yes, so you have understood it.
fact: Neighbourly means friendly and helpful, the way a good neighbour is.
fact: «Neighbourly» comes from «neighbour» with «-ly» on the end, like «friendly».
fact: Helping next door, such as taking in a parcel or checking on an elderly neighbour, is a neighbourly thing to do.
fact: In American spelling, the word is written «neighborly», without the «u». It means the same thing.
fact: Neighbourly can also be formal, meaning to do with neighbours: neighbourly relations.
exercise: «It was very neighbourly of Mrs Okafor to bring us soup when we were ill.» What does neighbourly mean here? | *Friendly and helpful | Far away and hard to find | Noisy and rude | Angry about the noise
exercise: «Tom and his dad had a neighbourly chat over the garden fence.» What kind of chat was it? | *Friendly and easy | Secret and silent | Loud and angry | Long and boring
exercise: «The council wants good neighbourly relations on our street.» What are neighbourly relations? | Tall fences around the gardens | *Friendly ties between neighbours | Lists of local shops | Rules about parking cars
test: «The new family were not very neighbourly and kept their curtains shut.» What does this suggest about them? | They were very friendly to everyone | They loved the neighbours' pets | They were away at the shops | *They were unfriendly and kept to themselves
test: Which of these is a neighbourly thing to do? | Running away when your neighbour says hello | Painting your neighbour's wall without asking | *Taking in your neighbour's parcel | Moving your neighbour's bin
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to neighbourly in «a kind, helpful neighbour»? | *Kind | Loud | Quiet | Tall
